<h2>Check before you upload</h2>
<p>Two tests take ten seconds and catch most bad thumbnails. <b>The squint test</b>: look at it at 168px. If the word cannot be read or the subject cannot be named, it fails. <b>The grey test</b>: take the colour away. If the hierarchy disappears, it was resting on colour, and colour is the first thing a busy feed drowns.</p>
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="thumb-scale">
	<figure>
		<div class="im-poster im-poster-number">
			<span class="im-poster-figure">7</span>
			<strong class="im-poster-word">tools I use daily<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
			<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/face-sunglasses.jpg" alt="">
		</div>
		<figcaption>full size</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure class="thumb-tiny">
		<div class="im-poster im-poster-number">
			<span class="im-poster-figure">7</span>
			<strong class="im-poster-word">tools I use daily<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
			<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/person-reading.jpg" alt="">
		</div>
		<figcaption>168px — a phone's list</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure class="thumb-tiny">
		<div class="im-poster im-poster-number thumb-gray">
			<span class="im-poster-figure">7</span>
			<strong class="im-poster-word">tools I use daily<i class="im-poster-dot"></i></strong>
			<img class="im-poster-subject im-poster-card" src="/assets/photos/person-backpack.jpg" alt="">
		</div>
		<figcaption>no colour</figcaption>
	</figure>
</div>
{{/example}}
<ul>
	<li>Does it say something the title does not?</li>
	<li>Is there one thing that is clearly biggest?</li>
	<li>Is the bottom-right corner empty?</li>
	<li>Is the red used once (plus the dot)?</li>
	<li>Does it look like the last three thumbnails on the channel?</li>
	<li>Does the video keep the promise in its first thirty seconds?</li>
</ul>
<p>When two ideas both pass, let the audience choose: YouTube Studio's <b>Test &amp; Compare</b> shows up to three thumbnails to different viewers and keeps the one watched longest. Change one thing between them — the word, or the subject — or the result says nothing.</p>

<h2>The classes</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster</code></td><td>The 16:9 canvas and its 16 × 9 grid. Every child fills it until a type places it.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-media</code> · <code>-tiles</code> · <code>-shade</code> · <code>-bar</code></td><td>Ground: a photo, a wall of photos, a scrim, a strip.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-subject</code> + <code>-card</code> · <code>-round</code></td><td>Subject and its shape. <code>--im-poster-focus</code> moves the crop.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-screen-frame</code></td><td>A window for a screenshot.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-word</code> + <code>-lg</code> · <code>im-poster-on-media</code></td><td>The word; <code>im-poster-dot</code> is its full stop.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-figure</code></td><td>A big number.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-chip</code> + <code>-paper</code> · <code>-ink</code> · <code>-end</code>, <code>im-poster-hand</code>, <code>im-poster-glyph</code>, <code>im-poster-disc</code>, <code>im-poster-ep</code></td><td>Marks.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-time</code></td><td>A stand-in for YouTube's timestamp, to design around.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-guides</code></td><td>Draws the grid, the thirds and the keep-clear corner.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-poster-face</code>, <code>-place</code>, <code>-screen</code>, <code>-ask</code>, <code>-split</code>, <code>-versus</code>, <code>-number</code>, <code>-recap</code>, <code>-type</code>, <code>-product</code>, <code>-icon</code></td><td>The eleven <a href="/concept/thumbnails/types/">types</a>.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
